#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# blend

#% text
# `blend([c1, c2, ...])` gives the average of the colours.

#% text
# `blend([c1, c2, ..., cn], t)` gives the colour a fraction t of the way along c1, c2, ..., cn, evenly spaced: c1 at 0, cn at 1.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Red, green, blue and opacity are mixed linearly; t is clipped to [0, 1].

#% item
# The result is an `rgb_color` with machine-real components.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# Halfway between red and blue:

#% cell
blend([red, blue])
#% output
#= rgb_color(0.5, 0.0, 0.5)

#% text
# Three quarters of the way along red, green, blue:

#% cell
blend([red, green, blue], 0.75)
#% output
#= rgb_color(0.0, 0.5, 0.5)

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# A colour ramp of rectangles:

#% cell
graphics(table([blend([blue, white, red], k/8), rectangle([k, 0])], k, range(0, 8)))
#% output
#= image("blend.files/blend-3.png")

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# Every element must be a colour:

#% cell
blend([red, 5])
#% output
#! failure(argument, blend, 1)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `lighter`, `darker`, `color_convert`, `hue`
